--mask-host's second layer for ai-jail 3.5.0 (from the fork's
feat/host-view-extra, merged into the Zeo stack zeo/ebuild-350-r3). Under
--mask-host the sandbox now also reads: the numeric kernel release only in
/proc/version and /proc/sys/kernel/{osrelease,version} (no distribution
suffix, builder, compiler or date); a generic os-release (ID=linux); a
/proc/swaps with no swap; its own boot id; empty /etc/crypttab, release
files and partition, disk, NUMA, memory-block, interrupt, scheduler and
pressure files; a tmpfs over /etc/portage, /sys/block, /usr/lib/modules and
/usr/src; CPU topology files, so lscpu reads one thread per core; a live
free-memory figure under a memory limit; and CLOCK_BOOTTIME,
CLOCK_MONOTONIC and sysinfo().uptime counted from the launch, in a time
namespace the supervisor enters before it execs bwrap. Every jail: the
landlock helper drops AI_JAIL_QUIET before the final exec. New opt-in
--overlay-system (with --mask-host): /usr, /etc and /opt through read-only
overlays so the mount table names no host disk for them. Must follow
ai-jail-mask-host.patch. Design: zeo-workspace docs/HOST-VIEW-EXTRA-LAYER.md §4.2.

